        "questionHtml": "<section class=\"listening-source-group\" data-question-start=\"31\" data-question-end=\"40\" data-question-type=\"sentence-completion\"><header class=\"listening-source-header\"><p class=\"listening-source-range\">Questions 31-40</p><p class=\"listening-source-instruction\">Complete the notes below. Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS.</p></header><div class=\"listening-source-note-block\"><div class=\"listening-source-note-row\"><strong>Mass Strandings of Whales and Dolphins</strong></div><div class=\"listening-source-note-row\">Mass strandings: situations where groups of whales, dolphins, etc. swim onto the beach and die</div><div class=\"listening-source-note-row\">Common in areas where the  <span aria-label=\"Blank for question 31\" class=\"listening-answer-blank\" data-question=\"31\" role=\"img\"><span class=\"listening-answer-number\">(31)</span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"listening-answer-line\"> </span></span> can change quickly</div></div><div class=\"listening-source-note-block\"><div class=\"listening-source-note-row\"><strong>Several other theories:</strong></div><div class=\"listening-source-note-row\"><strong>Parasites</strong></div><div class=\"listening-source-note-row\">e.g. some parasites can affect marine animals’ <span aria-label=\"Blank for question 32\" class=\"listening-answer-blank\" data-question=\"32\" role=\"img\"><span class=\"listening-answer-number\">(32)</span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"listening-answer-line\"> </span></span> ,which they depend on for navigation</div></div><div class=\"listening-source-note-block\"><div class=\"listening-source-note-row\"><strong>Toxins</strong></div><div class=\"listening-source-note-row\">Poisons from <span aria-label=\"Blank for question 33\" class=\"listening-answer-blank\" data-question=\"33\" role=\"img\"><span class=\"listening-answer-number\">(33)</span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"listening-answer-line\"> </span></span> or <span aria-label=\"Additional blank for question 33\" class=\"listening-answer-blank listening-answer-blank-continuation\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"listening-answer-line\"> </span></span> are commonly consumed by whales</div><div class=\"listening-source-note-row\">e.g. Cape Cod (1988) – whales were killed by saxitoxin</div></div><div class=\"listening-source-note-block\"><div class=\"listening-source-note-row\"><strong>Accidental Strandings</strong></div><div class=\"listening-source-note-row\">Animals may follow prey ashore, e.g. Thurston (1995)</div><div class=\"listening-source-note-row\">Unlikely because the majority of animals were not  <span aria-label=\"Blank for question 34\" class=\"listening-answer-blank\" data-question=\"34\" role=\"img\"><span class=\"listening-answer-number\">(34)</span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"listening-answer-line\"> </span></span> when they stranded</div></div><div class=\"listening-source-question-list\" role=\"list\"><div class=\"listening-source-question-row\" data-question-row=\"35\" role=\"listitem\"><strong>Human Activity</strong><span aria-label=\"Blank for question 35\" class=\"listening-answer-blank\" data-question=\"35\" role=\"img\"><span class=\"listening-answer-number\">(35)</span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"listening-answer-line\"> </span></span> from military tests are linked to some recent strandings</div><div class=\"listening-source-support-row\">The Bahamas (2000) stranding was unusual because the whales</div><div class=\"listening-source-question-row\" data-question-row=\"36\" role=\"listitem\">• were all  <span aria-label=\"Blank for question 36\" class=\"listening-answer-blank\" data-question=\"36\" role=\"img\"><span class=\"listening-answer-number\">(36)</span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"listening-answer-line\"> </span></span></div><div class=\"listening-source-question-row\" data-question-row=\"37\" role=\"listitem\">• were not in a  <span aria-label=\"Blank for question 37\" class=\"listening-answer-blank\" data-question=\"37\" role=\"img\"><span class=\"listening-answer-number\">(37)</span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"listening-answer-line\"> </span></span></div></div><div class=\"listening-source-question-list\" role=\"list\"><p class=\"listening-source-title\"><strong>Group Behaviour</strong></p><div class=\"listening-source-question-row\" data-question-row=\"38\" role=\"listitem\">• More standings in the most  <span aria-label=\"Blank for question 38\" class=\"listening-answer-blank\" data-question=\"38\" role=\"img\"><span class=\"listening-answer-number\">(38)</span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"listening-answer-line\"> </span></span> species of whales</div><div class=\"listening-source-question-row\" data-question-row=\"39\" role=\"listitem\">• 1994 dolphin stranding – only the  <span aria-label=\"Blank for question 39\" class=\"listening-answer-blank\" data-question=\"39\" role=\"img\"><span class=\"listening-answer-number\">(39)</span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"listening-answer-line\"> </span></span> was ill</div></div><div class=\"listening-source-note-block\"><div class=\"listening-source-note-row\"><strong>Further Reading</strong></div><div class=\"listening-source-note-row\">Marine Mammals Ashore (Connor) – gives information about stranding  <span aria-label=\"Blank for question 40\" class=\"listening-answer-blank\" data-question=\"40\" role=\"img\"><span class=\"listening-answer-number\">(40)</span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"listening-answer-line\"> </span></span></div></div></section>",
        "startSeconds": 1199.24,
